inputs:
{"Query": "Give me a word problem exercise for a 7th grade student learning algebra. It should be an exercise on solving equations with variables on both sides.", "Answer": "Alvin had 20 oranges. He gave some oranges to Roy and had 8 left. Roy had 16 oranges. How many oranges did Alvin give to Roy?

Let \( x \) represent the number of oranges Alvin gave to Roy. Set up an equation based on the given information and solve for \( x \).

\begin{equation*}
20 - x = 8
\end{equation*}

Solving for \( x \) gives:

\begin{equation*}
x = 20 - 8
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
x = 12
\end{equation*}

Alvin gave Roy 12 oranges."}

{"Query": "Give me a true or false exercise for a student learning physics. It should be an exercise on Newton's laws of motion.", "Answer": "What is the acceleration of a 2000 kg car if a 1000 N force is applied to it?

\begin{equation*}
\text{Acceleration} = \frac{\text{Force}}{\text{Mass}} = \frac{1000 \text{ N}}{2000 \text{ kg}} = \_\_\_ \text{m/s}^2
\end{equation*}"}

{"Query": "Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should have a subsection for hints.", "Answer": "The usual selling prices of a handbag and a set of jewellery were \$990 and \$550 respectively. Jane bought them at a 10\% discount during a sale. How much did she pay altogether?

\subsection*{Answers}
Jane paid \$1,386 altogether."}

{"Query": "Give me an arithmetic exercise for a 5th grade student learning mathematics. It should have a subsection for hints. It should be an exercise on long division.", "Answer": "Sofia has \( \frac{3}{4} \) of a cake. She divides the cake into three pieces and eats one of the pieces. What fraction of Sofia's cake is left? Show your working.

\subsection*{Answers}
Sofia has \( \frac{3}{4} \) of a cake. After dividing it into three pieces, each piece is \( \frac{3}{4} \div 3 = \frac{3}{12} = \frac{1}{4} \). After eating one piece, she has \( \frac{3}{4} - \frac{1}{4} = \frac{2}{4} = \frac{1}{2} \) of the cake left."}

{"Query": "Give me a combination of a punctuation exercise and a writing exercise for a 3rd grade student learning German. It should be an exercise on direct speech sentences.", "Answer": "Copy and punctuate these direct speech sentences.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Rose said We are your new neighbours.
\item We should make them feel welcome said Father Mouse.
\item Shall we invite them for tea asked Mother Mouse.
\end{enumerate}"}

{"Query": "Give me a combination of a word scramble exercise and a translation exercise for a student learning Spanish. It should have a subsection for answers, and hints.", "Answer": "All the letters of these words are jumbled up. Rearrange the letters so that they make meaningful words.
\begin{enumerate}
\item neniusatal
\item stwgeee
\item eensegmnt
\item ceshrt
\item nburi
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Hints}

\begin{enumerate}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{a}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{connect}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{g}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{been}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{s}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{segment}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{r}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{right}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{b}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{brown}
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item aansluiten
\item geweest
\item segmenten
\item rechts
\item bruin
\end{enumerate}"}

{"Query": "Give me a combination of a creative exercise and a short answer exercise for a 10th grade student learning computer science. It should be an exercise on designing a robot.", "Answer": "Invent your own robot which would help with cleaning. Think of a name for your robot. List the main functions of your robot and the advantages of using it to do the cleaning.

\paragraph{Think With Me}
Is your robot cleaner humanoid or not? Why did you make that choice?

\paragraph{Bonus Activity}
Design a poster to advertise the new robot cleaner."}

